  "details": "Description\n\nAfter the last update, every time an avatar goes past \"server processing\" and starts downloading the entire game mimics the moment right before a crash, with everything and everyone stopping and the game only resuming after the download is done.\n\nReproduction Steps\n\nBe in any instance with other people. Have one of those people start switching avatars to something that is not in the cache and watch the entire game basically freeze while you can watch the download processes. Once it gets past the actual download the game catches up and resumes as normal.\n\nDetails\n\n- Category: Networking\n\n- Frequency: Always\n\n---\n\nplatform: PC (platform: Windows, store: Steam, headset: None)\n\nrawPlatform: WindowsPlayer\n\nclientVersion: 2026.3.3p2-1921-15c4a824b2-Release\n\nunityVersion: 6000.0.67f1-DWR\n\nIn-Client Report",
